### Works in IntelliJ (Ultimate/HTTP Client) and VS Code (REST Client extension).
### You can also paste the URLs into a browser (GET only) or use Postman.

### 1. Skeleton check
GET http://localhost:8080/api/hello

### 2. All properties
GET http://localhost:8080/api/properties

### 3. Filters (same as React search box, dropdown, max price)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/properties?status=For Rent&maxPrice=30000
###
GET http://localhost:8080/api/properties?search=pune

### 4. One property
GET http://localhost:8080/api/properties/1

### 5. Not found -> 404 with JSON error
GET http://localhost:8080/api/properties/999

### 6. Create -> 201
POST http://localhost:8080/api/properties
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Test Loft",
  "price": 5500000,
  "location": "Pune",
  "bedrooms": 2,
  "bathrooms": 1,
  "area": 900,
  "type": "Apartment",
  "status": "For Sale",
  "imageUrl": "https://picsum.photos/id/1040/600/400",
  "description": "Created through the API",
  "agentId": 1
}

### 7. Business rule broken (price 0) -> 400
POST http://localhost:8080/api/properties
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Bad", "price": 0, "status": "For Sale" }

### 8. Update (change the id to the one you created)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/properties/7
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Test Loft (updated)",
  "price": 5000000,
  "location": "Pune",
  "bedrooms": 2,
  "bathrooms": 1,
  "area": 900,
  "type": "Apartment",
  "status": "For Sale",
  "imageUrl": "https://picsum.photos/id/1040/600/400",
  "description": "Updated through the API",
  "agentId": 1
}

### 9. Delete -> 204   (deleting id 1 gives 409 because it has inquiries)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/properties/7
